// activities.js: the classroom activities, games and teaching techniques the MLT books describe, one entry each.
// Global MLTActivities (array). Read by mlt-walk.js (the book pages link steps to these) and mlt/activities.qmd (filterable list).
//
// The site does not reproduce the books: each entry is a name, a short description in this site's words, and the
// pages where the book describes it, so the teacher can open the book there.
//
// Entry:
//   id       unique slug
//   name     what the book calls it (or a short name of ours when the book has none)
//   kind     technique (how to run an LSA or class) | game | movement | instruments | singing | bridge (to an inference skill)
//   skill    MLT skill levels it serves: "A/O", "VA", "PS", "SA", "CS", "G-a/o", "G-v", "G-s", "C/I-a/o", "C/I-s", "TU" ...
//   content  "tonal" | "rhythm" (or both); tonality / meter if the book ties it to one: "major", "minor", "duple", "triple"
//   props    things you need (puppet, scarves, Boomwhackers ...)
//   credit   person the author credits with the idea
//   how      what you do (teacher's view), in our words
//   student  the instruction a student sees (student view), or null when it is only a teacher technique
//   refs     [{ book, p }] book id (mlt-walk.js BOOKS) and print page(s)
//   tunes    tune ids (%%id in the tune collection, practice/tunes.html?tune=<id>) the book uses with it
//   tool     a site page that does it in the browser, if there is one
//   mins     typical length in minutes (the lesson planner uses it); set below: from the book where it gives a time
//            (minsFrom "book"), otherwise an estimate by kind (minsFrom "estimate"). Techniques get null: they run inside
//            another part of the lesson, not as a slot of their own.
//   screen   what the class TV shows (lesson-builder.js class screen): "song" (the tunes, large), "tool" (the site page
//            in a frame), "prompt" (the student line in large type), "timer" (a big timer only), or null (nothing extra).
//            Set below from tunes / tool / student unless an entry gives its own.
//
// Pages: Mullen's printed page numbers (= the PDF's page numbers in this book), found by matching the text cache line by line
// against the PDF's own page text (research_notes/mlt-sources/text/MLTAnyMusicTeacherCanDuDe.pages.txt, made with PDFKit).
